        <h2 class="k-legal__part" id="part-a-introduction">PART A — INTRODUCTION</h2>
            <h3 id="sec-1">1. Definitions</h3>
            <p>For the purpose of these Terms:</p>
            <h4>1.1 Platform</h4>
            <p>"Platform" means the Kaarigar website, mobile applications, software applications, dashboards, APIs, communication systems, and all related products and services operated by Kaarigar.</p>
            <h4>1.2 Company</h4>
            <p>"Kaarigar", "Company", "We", "Us" or "Our" means Kaarigar Technologies, including its subsidiaries, affiliates, successors and assigns.</p>
            <h4>1.3 Employer</h4>
            <p>An Employer means any business, company, partnership, LLP, proprietorship, organization, institution, government entity, startup, MSME, enterprise, contractor, facility management company, restaurant, hotel, warehouse, retail business, hospital, manufacturer, logistics company, event organizer, commercial establishment or any other entity that registers on the Platform for the purpose of discovering, engaging or communicating with workers.</p>
            <h4>1.4 Worker</h4>
            <p>A Worker means any individual who creates a profile on the Platform for the purpose of discovering, applying for, accepting or performing work opportunities.</p>
            <h4>1.5 User</h4>
            <p>A User includes every person or entity accessing or using the Platform, including Employers, Workers, visitors, administrators and authorized representatives.</p>
            <h4>1.6 Job</h4>
            <p>A Job means any work opportunity, including hourly work, shifts, daily work, temporary assignments, contract work, project-based work or permanent employment opportunities posted by an Employer.</p>
            <h4>1.7 Shift</h4>
            <p>A Shift means a specific work period defined by an Employer, including start time, end time, location and payment.</p>
            <h4>1.8 Content</h4>
            <p>Content includes text, images, videos, documents, resumes, company information, ratings, reviews, comments, messages and all other information uploaded or published on the Platform.</p>
            <h4>1.9 Applicable Law</h4>
            <p>Applicable Law means all Central, State and local laws, rules, regulations, government notifications, judicial orders and statutory requirements applicable to the User and/or the Platform.</p>
            <h3 id="sec-2">2. Acceptance of Terms</h3>
            <p>By accessing or using the Platform, you represent and warrant that:</p>
            <ul><li>You have read these Terms.</li><li>You understand these Terms.</li><li>You agree to comply with these Terms.</li><li>You are legally capable of entering into binding agreements.</li><li>You will comply with all applicable laws while using the Platform.</li><li>If you do not agree, you must immediately discontinue use of the Platform.</li></ul>
            <h3 id="sec-3">3. About Kaarigar</h3>
            <p>Kaarigar operates India's On-Demand B2B Workforce Platform, enabling businesses to connect with workers for hourly shifts, temporary assignments, project-based engagements and permanent hiring opportunities across multiple industries.</p>
            <p>The Platform uses technology to facilitate workforce discovery, communication and matching between Employers and Workers.</p>
            <h3 id="sec-4">4. Nature of the Platform</h3>
            <h4>4.1 Technology Marketplace</h4>
            <p>Kaarigar operates as a technology-enabled online marketplace.</p>
            <p>The Platform enables Employers and Workers to discover each other, communicate and engage directly.</p>
            <h4>4.2 No Guarantee of Engagement</h4>
            <p>Kaarigar does not guarantee that:</p>
            <ul><li>an Employer will hire a Worker;</li><li>a Worker will accept a Job;</li><li>any Job will be completed;</li><li>any User will receive a specific number of opportunities;</li><li>any User will achieve particular business outcomes.</li></ul>
            <h4>4.3 Marketplace Only</h4>
            <p>Unless expressly agreed in writing through a separate agreement, Kaarigar provides only the technology platform and does not itself provide workforce, staffing, recruitment, payroll or outsourcing services.</p>
            <h3 id="sec-5">5. Eligibility</h3>
            <p>To use the Platform:</p>
            <ul><li>Individuals must be legally competent to enter into binding contracts under applicable law.</li><li>Businesses must have the legal authority to operate and register.</li><li>Users must provide accurate and complete information.</li><li>Users must not be prohibited by law from using the Platform.</li><li>Kaarigar may refuse or suspend access if eligibility requirements are not met.</li></ul>
            <h3 id="sec-6">6. User Accounts</h3>
            <p>Users must create an account to access certain features of the Platform.</p>
            <p>Each User shall:</p>
            <ul><li>provide true, accurate and complete information;</li><li>maintain the accuracy of account information;</li><li>promptly update any changes;</li><li>keep login credentials confidential;</li><li>be responsible for all activities conducted through their account.</li><li>Users must not share accounts or create accounts on behalf of another person without authorization.</li></ul>
            <h3 id="sec-7">7. Verification</h3>
            <p>Kaarigar may require identity verification, business verification, document verification or other checks before granting access to certain features.</p>
            <p>Verification by Kaarigar indicates only that certain information or documents have been reviewed to the extent of the verification process adopted by the Platform. It does not constitute a certification, endorsement or guarantee regarding the identity, qualifications, experience, suitability, reliability or conduct of any User.</p>
            <p>Users remain responsible for conducting their own assessment before entering into any engagement.</p>
            <h3 id="sec-8">8. Account Security</h3>
            <p>Users are solely responsible for maintaining the confidentiality of their account credentials and for all activities occurring under their account.</p>
            <p>Users must immediately notify Kaarigar if they become aware of any unauthorized access, suspected compromise or misuse of their account.</p>
            <p>Kaarigar reserves the right to suspend or restrict access where it reasonably believes that account security has been compromised or that the account is being used in violation of these Terms.</p>
            <h2 class="k-legal__part" id="part-b-marketplace-model">PART B — MARKETPLACE MODEL</h2>
            <h3 id="sec-9">9. Marketplace Services</h3>
            <h4>9.1 Nature of Services</h4>
            <p>Kaarigar is a technology-enabled online marketplace that facilitates the discovery, communication, and engagement between businesses seeking workforce and individuals seeking work opportunities.</p>
            <p>The Platform enables users to:</p>
            <ul><li>Register and create user profiles.</li><li>Post workforce requirements.</li><li>Search for workers or jobs.</li><li>Apply for work opportunities.</li><li>Communicate through the Platform.</li><li>Schedule work assignments.</li><li>Verify attendance through platform features.</li><li>Submit ratings and reviews.</li><li>Access related workforce management features introduced from time to time.</li></ul>
            <h4>9.2 Platform Role</h4>
            <p>Kaarigar provides only the technological infrastructure necessary to facilitate interactions between Users.</p>
            <p>Kaarigar does not participate in the negotiation, supervision, execution, or completion of work assignments unless expressly stated under a separate written agreement.</p>
            <h4>9.3 Independent Decisions</h4>
            <p>Employers independently decide:</p>
            <ul><li>whom to hire;</li><li>wages or compensation;</li><li>work schedules;</li><li>work location;</li><li>duties and responsibilities;</li><li>duration of engagement;</li><li>workplace policies.</li></ul>
            <p>Workers independently decide:</p>
            <ul><li>whether to register;</li><li>whether to apply;</li><li>whether to accept work;</li><li>availability;</li><li>preferred working hours;</li><li>willingness to continue an engagement.</li></ul>
            <h4>9.4 Platform Availability</h4>
            <p>Kaarigar does not guarantee uninterrupted access to the Platform.</p>
            <p>The Platform may be unavailable due to:</p>
            <ul><li>maintenance;</li><li>upgrades;</li><li>technical failures;</li><li>cyber security incidents;</li><li>force majeure events;</li><li>third-party service failures.</li></ul>
            <h3 id="sec-10">10. No Employment Relationship</h3>
            <h4>10.1 Marketplace Only</h4>
            <p>Kaarigar is not the employer of Workers using the Platform unless expressly agreed under a separate written agreement.</p>
            <p>The Platform merely facilitates introductions between Employers and Workers.</p>
            <h4>10.2 Employment Relationship</h4>
            <p>Any employment relationship, contractual engagement, consultancy, apprenticeship, freelance arrangement, temporary engagement, or other working relationship exists solely between the Employer and the Worker.</p>
            <h4>10.3 Employer Responsibilities</h4>
            <p>The Employer remains solely responsible for:</p>
            <ul><li>recruitment decisions;</li><li>interviews;</li><li>selection;</li><li>appointment;</li><li>wages;</li><li>overtime;</li><li>incentives;</li><li>bonuses;</li><li>leave;</li><li>disciplinary actions;</li><li>workplace safety;</li><li>statutory compliances;</li><li>termination;</li><li>employee benefits.</li></ul>
            <h4>10.4 Worker Responsibilities</h4>
            <p>Workers remain solely responsible for:</p>
            <ul><li>accepting work voluntarily;</li><li>performing assigned duties;</li><li>complying with workplace rules;</li><li>maintaining professional conduct;</li><li>complying with applicable laws.</li></ul>
            <h4>10.5 No Employer Status</h4>
            <p>Nothing contained in these Terms shall be interpreted as creating an employer—employee relationship between Kaarigar and any Worker solely because the Worker uses the Platform.</p>
            <h3 id="sec-11">11. No Principal Employer Relationship</h3>
            <h4>11.1 Platform Role</h4>
            <p>Unless expressly agreed through a separate written commercial agreement, Kaarigar does not act as the Principal Employer in respect of work engagements facilitated through the Platform.</p>
            <h4>11.2 Independent Engagement</h4>
            <p>Employers independently engage Workers through the Platform.</p>
            <p>The Employer remains responsible for all obligations arising from such engagement under applicable law.</p>
            <h4>11.3 No Control Over Work</h4>
            <p>Kaarigar does not ordinarily:</p>
            <ul><li>supervise work;</li><li>allocate daily tasks;</li><li>control work execution;</li><li>approve leave;</li><li>issue employment instructions;</li><li>manage attendance outside Platform features;</li><li>exercise disciplinary authority.</li></ul>
            <h4>11.4 Compliance Responsibility</h4>
            <p>Compliance with labour, employment, wage, social security, occupational safety, taxation, and other applicable laws remains the responsibility of the Employer engaging the Worker, unless otherwise agreed in writing.</p>
            <h3 id="sec-12">12. No Labour Contractor Relationship</h3>
            <h4>12.1 Marketplace Platform</h4>
            <p>Kaarigar operates as a technology marketplace and not as a labour contractor in the ordinary course of Platform operations.</p>
            <h4>12.2 No Supply of Labour</h4>
            <p>Kaarigar does not itself recruit, deploy, assign, supervise, or supply manpower to Employers through the Platform unless a separate written agreement specifically provides for such services.</p>
            <h4>12.3 No Payroll Services</h4>
            <p>Unless separately contracted, Kaarigar does not:</p>
            <ul><li>process salaries;</li><li>maintain attendance;</li><li>administer payroll;</li><li>deduct statutory contributions;</li><li>manage employment benefits;</li><li>provide labour compliance services.</li></ul>
            <h4>12.4 Separate Commercial Agreements</h4>
            <p>If Kaarigar enters into a separate agreement to provide staffing, payroll, outsourcing, or employer-of-record services, that agreement shall govern those services independently of these Terms.</p>
            <h3 id="sec-13">13. No Agency Relationship</h3>
            <p>Nothing in these Terms shall be construed to create:</p>
            <ul><li>partnership;</li><li>joint venture;</li><li>agency;</li><li>franchise;</li><li>fiduciary relationship;</li><li>employment relationship;</li><li>representative authority,</li><li>between Kaarigar and any User.</li><li>No User has authority to bind Kaarigar to any contract, representation, or obligation unless expressly authorized in writing.</li></ul>
            <h3 id="sec-14">14. User Responsibilities</h3>
            <h4>14.1 General Responsibilities</h4>
            <p>Every User agrees to:</p>
            <ul><li>provide accurate information;</li><li>comply with applicable laws;</li><li>use the Platform honestly;</li><li>respect other Users;</li><li>maintain account security;</li><li>promptly update profile information;</li><li>avoid misuse of the Platform.</li></ul>
            <h4>14.2 Accuracy of Information</h4>
            <p>Users are solely responsible for ensuring that all information submitted on the Platform is true, accurate, complete, and current.</p>
            <p>Providing false, misleading, forged, or incomplete information may result in suspension or termination of the account.</p>
            <h4>14.3 Independent Evaluation</h4>
            <p>Employers and Workers acknowledge that they are responsible for independently evaluating the suitability, qualifications, experience, reputation, and reliability of the other party before entering into any engagement.</p>
            <p>Kaarigar does not guarantee the accuracy of user-provided information beyond any verification process expressly described by the Platform.</p>
            <h4>14.4 Compliance with Laws</h4>
            <p>Users must comply with all applicable laws, regulations, permits, licences, and contractual obligations relevant to their use of the Platform and any work engagement.</p>
            <h4>14.5 Prohibited Use</h4>
            <p>Users shall not use the Platform to:</p>
            <ul><li>engage in illegal or fraudulent activities;</li><li>post misleading or deceptive information;</li><li>discriminate unlawfully;</li><li>harass, threaten, or abuse other users;</li><li>upload malicious software or harmful code;</li><li>attempt unauthorized access to the Platform;</li><li>interfere with the operation or security of the Platform;</li><li>misuse personal data obtained through the Platform.</li><li>Violation of these obligations may result in suspension, termination, legal action, or reporting to the appropriate authorities.</li></ul>
            <h2 class="k-legal__part" id="part-c-employer-terms">PART C — EMPLOYER TERMS</h2>
            <h3 id="sec-15">15. Employer Registration</h3>
            <h4>15.1 Eligibility</h4>
            <p>To register as an Employer on Kaarigar, you must:</p>
            <p>Be at least 18 years of age or otherwise legally competent to enter into binding contracts under applicable law.</p>
            <p>If registering on behalf of an entity, be duly authorized to bind that entity.</p>
            <p>Provide complete, accurate, and up-to-date information during registration.</p>
            <p>Comply with all applicable laws, regulations, and licensing requirements relevant to your business.</p>
            <p>Kaarigar reserves the right to refuse, suspend, or terminate registration where the eligibility criteria are not met or where information provided is inaccurate or misleading.</p>
            <h4>15.2 Business Information</h4>
            <p>Employers may be required to provide, where applicable:</p>
            <ul><li>Business or Trade Name</li><li>Legal Entity Name</li><li>Business Registration Number (if applicable)</li><li>GSTIN (if applicable)</li><li>PAN</li><li>Registered Office Address</li><li>Branch Address</li><li>Contact Person Details</li><li>Mobile Number</li><li>Email Address</li><li>Company Logo</li><li>Nature of Business</li><li>Industry Category</li><li>Number of Employees</li><li>Authorized Representative Details</li><li>Any other information reasonably required for verification or platform operations</li></ul>
            <p>Kaarigar may verify the authenticity of such information but does not guarantee the legal status or reputation of any Employer.</p>
            <h4>15.3 Verification</h4>
            <p>Kaarigar may request supporting documents for business verification, such as:</p>
            <ul><li>GST Registration</li><li>PAN</li><li>Certificate of Incorporation</li><li>Partnership Deed</li><li>Shop &amp; Establishment Registration</li><li>MSME Registration</li><li>Trade Licence</li><li>Authorized Signatory Identification</li><li>Any other documents deemed necessary</li></ul>
            <p>Verification by Kaarigar signifies only that certain information or documents have been reviewed. It is not an endorsement, certification, guarantee, or representation regarding the Employer's financial standing, legal compliance, or business practices.</p>
            <h4>15.4 Authorized Users</h4>
            <p>An Employer may authorize employees or representatives to access the Platform on its behalf.</p>
            <p>The Employer is responsible for ensuring that such users comply with these Terms and remains liable for all activities performed through its account.</p>
            <h3 id="sec-16">16. Posting Jobs</h3>
            <h4>16.1 Accuracy of Job Information</h4>
            <p>Employers must ensure that all job postings are accurate, complete, and truthful.</p>
            <p>Job postings should clearly specify, where applicable:</p>
            <ul><li>Job Title</li><li>Industry</li><li>Location</li><li>Shift Date</li><li>Start Time</li><li>End Time</li><li>Duration</li><li>Number of Workers Required</li><li>Skills Required</li><li>Experience Required</li><li>Compensation</li><li>Overtime (if applicable)</li><li>Uniform or Safety Equipment (if applicable)</li><li>Reporting Instructions</li><li>Contact Person (where permitted)</li></ul>
            <h4>16.2 Lawful Jobs Only</h4>
            <p>Employers shall post only lawful work opportunities.</p>
            <p>Jobs must not:</p>
            <ul><li>Violate applicable laws.</li><li>Involve child labour.</li><li>Involve bonded or forced labour.</li><li>Require illegal activities.</li><li>Promote discrimination.</li><li>Endanger health or safety without lawful safeguards.</li><li>Misrepresent wages or working conditions.</li></ul>
            <p>Kaarigar reserves the right to reject or remove any job that, in its sole discretion, violates these Terms or applicable law.</p>
            <h4>16.3 Employer Responsibility for Job Content</h4>
            <p>Employers are solely responsible for:</p>
            <ul><li>The accuracy of job descriptions.</li><li>Compensation details.</li><li>Working conditions.</li><li>Workplace safety.</li><li>Compliance with statutory obligations.</li><li>Representations made to workers.</li><li>Kaarigar is not responsible for reviewing or validating every job posting.</li></ul>
            <h4>16.4 Job Modifications</h4>
            <p>Employers may edit or update job postings before workers are engaged, subject to platform functionality and applicable policies.</p>
            <p>Material changes to a job after worker acceptance should be communicated promptly. Workers may decline materially altered assignments.</p>
            <h4>16.5 Job Cancellation</h4>
            <p>Employers may cancel job postings in accordance with Kaarigar's Cancellation &amp; Refund Policy.</p>
            <p>Repeated cancellations, especially after workers have accepted assignments, may lead to restrictions, penalties, or suspension of the Employer account.</p>
            <h3 id="sec-17">17. Employer Obligations</h3>
            <p>Employers agree to:</p>
            <ul><li>Treat workers with dignity and respect.</li><li>Provide a safe and lawful working environment.</li><li>Communicate honestly.</li><li>Honour agreed compensation.</li><li>Comply with all applicable laws.</li><li>Maintain professional conduct.</li><li>Cooperate during investigations of complaints or disputes.</li><li>Use the Platform in good faith.</li></ul>
            <h4>17.1 Workplace Safety</h4>
            <p>Employers are responsible for providing, where applicable:</p>
            <ul><li>Safe working conditions.</li><li>Necessary safety equipment.</li><li>Job-specific training or instructions.</li><li>Emergency procedures.</li><li>Compliance with occupational health and safety laws.</li></ul>
            <h4>17.2 Equal Opportunity</h4>
            <p>Employers shall not discriminate unlawfully on the basis of race, caste, religion, sex, disability, age, or any other protected characteristic under applicable law.</p>
            <p>Where a role has genuine occupational requirements permitted by law, such requirements should be clearly stated.</p>
