            <p>Kaarigar may suspend, restrict, or terminate Employer accounts for violations of these Terms and may report unlawful conduct to appropriate authorities where required.</p>
            <h2 class="k-legal__part" id="part-d-worker-terms">PART D — WORKER TERMS</h2>
            <h3 id="sec-21">21. Worker Registration</h3>
            <h4>21.1 Eligibility</h4>
            <p>To register as a Worker on the Platform, you must:</p>
            <ul><li>Be legally eligible to work under the applicable laws of India.</li><li>Be at least 18 years of age or otherwise legally competent to enter into binding contracts.</li><li>Provide true, complete, and accurate information during registration.</li><li>Maintain updated profile information.</li><li>Comply with these Terms of Use and all applicable laws.</li><li>Kaarigar reserves the right to reject, suspend, or terminate registrations that do not meet these eligibility requirements.</li></ul>
            <h4>21.2 Worker Profile</h4>
            <p>Workers may be required to provide:</p>
            <ul><li>Full Name</li><li>Mobile Number</li><li>Email Address (optional where permitted)</li><li>Photograph</li><li>Date of Birth</li><li>Gender (optional)</li><li>Residential Address</li><li>Current City</li><li>Preferred Work Locations</li><li>Skills</li><li>Experience</li><li>Languages Known</li><li>Education</li><li>Availability</li><li>Bank Account Details (where applicable)</li><li>UPI ID (where applicable)</li><li>Emergency Contact (optional)</li><li>Government-issued Identity Documents</li><li>Any other information reasonably required for verification or platform operations</li><li>Workers are responsible for ensuring that all information remains accurate and up to date.</li></ul>
            <h4>21.3 Verification</h4>
            <p>Kaarigar may verify certain information provided by Workers, including identity, contact details, or supporting documents.</p>
            <p>Verification does not constitute a guarantee of the Worker's qualifications, skills, character, conduct, suitability, or performance.</p>
            <p>Employers remain responsible for independently evaluating Workers before engagement.</p>
            <h4>21.4 Profile Visibility</h4>
            <p>By creating a Worker profile, you acknowledge that certain profile information may be visible to Employers for the purpose of evaluating work opportunities.</p>
            <p>Kaarigar will process and display such information in accordance with its Privacy Policy.</p>
            <h3 id="sec-22">22. Worker Responsibilities</h3>
            <p>Workers agree to:</p>
            <ul><li>Provide accurate information.</li><li>Maintain updated profiles.</li><li>Accept only those assignments they genuinely intend to perform.</li><li>Report to work on time.</li><li>Perform assigned duties with reasonable skill, care, and professionalism.</li><li>Follow lawful workplace rules and safety instructions.</li><li>Respect Employers, fellow workers, and customers.</li><li>Protect confidential business information.</li><li>Use the Platform honestly and responsibly.</li></ul>
            <h4>22.1 Professional Conduct</h4>
            <p>Workers shall:</p>
            <ul><li>Behave professionally.</li><li>Maintain appropriate workplace etiquette.</li><li>Follow reasonable workplace instructions.</li><li>Use safety equipment where required.</li><li>Maintain personal hygiene where relevant to the role.</li><li>Avoid disruptive or abusive behaviour.</li></ul>
            <h4>22.2 Compliance with Laws</h4>
            <p>Workers are responsible for complying with all applicable laws, regulations, permits, licences, and contractual obligations relevant to the work they undertake.</p>
            <h3 id="sec-23">23. Accepting Jobs</h3>
            <h4>23.1 Independent Choice</h4>
            <p>Workers are free to choose whether to apply for or accept work opportunities.</p>
            <p>Nothing in these Terms obligates a Worker to accept any particular assignment.</p>
            <h4>23.2 Commitment</h4>
            <p>Once a Worker accepts a job, the Worker agrees to make reasonable efforts to complete the engagement as agreed, unless prevented by circumstances beyond their reasonable control.</p>
            <h4>23.3 Accurate Availability</h4>
            <p>Workers should maintain accurate availability information to improve the quality of matching and reduce unnecessary cancellations.</p>
            <h4>23.4 Cancellations by Workers</h4>
            <p>Workers should cancel accepted assignments only where genuinely necessary.</p>
            <p>Repeated cancellations, particularly at short notice, may result in:</p>
            <ul><li>Reduced visibility on the Platform.</li><li>Temporary restrictions.</li><li>Account suspension.</li><li>Other actions permitted under these Terms.</li></ul>
            <h3 id="sec-24">24. Attendance and Shift Management</h3>
            <h4>24.1 Reporting to Work</h4>
            <p>Workers are expected to report to the designated location at the agreed reporting time.</p>
            <h4>24.2 Punctuality</h4>
            <p>Repeated late arrivals may affect a Worker's ratings, reliability score, or eligibility for future opportunities.</p>
            <h4>24.3 Early Departure</h4>
            <p>Workers should not leave an assignment before completion without the Employer's approval, except in emergencies or where continuing the work would be unlawful or unsafe.</p>
            <h4>24.4 No-Show</h4>
            <p>Failure to report for an accepted assignment without reasonable notice or justification may be treated as a "No-Show."</p>
            <p>Repeated No-Shows may result in warnings, reduced visibility, temporary suspension, or permanent removal from the Platform.</p>
            <h3 id="sec-25">25. OTP Verification</h3>
            <h4>25.1 Shift Start</h4>
            <p>Where the Platform uses OTP verification, the Worker must enter the Shift Start OTP at the work location to confirm commencement of the assignment.</p>
            <h4>25.2 Shift Completion</h4>
            <p>At the completion of the assignment, the Worker may be required to complete the Shift Completion OTP process in accordance with Platform procedures.</p>
            <h4>25.3 Accuracy</h4>
            <p>Workers must not misuse OTP verification or attempt to manipulate attendance records.</p>
            <p>Any fraudulent use of OTP features may result in immediate suspension or termination of the Worker's account.</p>
            <h3 id="sec-26">26. Ratings and Reviews</h3>
            <p>Following completion of an assignment, Employers may provide ratings and reviews based on their experience.</p>
            <p>Workers may also rate Employers where the Platform permits.</p>
            <p>Ratings should be:</p>
            <ul><li>Honest.</li><li>Fair.</li><li>Respectful.</li><li>Based on actual experience.</li><li>Kaarigar may remove ratings or reviews that violate these Terms or applicable law.</li></ul>
            <h3 id="sec-27">27. Worker Prohibited Conduct</h3>
            <p>Workers shall not:</p>
            <ul><li>Provide false or misleading information.</li><li>Use forged or altered documents.</li><li>Create multiple accounts without authorization.</li><li>Share accounts with others.</li><li>Impersonate another person.</li><li>Misrepresent skills or qualifications.</li><li>Accept assignments with no intention of attending.</li><li>Engage in fraud or deceptive practices.</li><li>Demand unauthorized payments.</li><li>Solicit work outside the Platform in violation of applicable Platform policies.</li><li>Harass, threaten, abuse, or discriminate against Employers or other users.</li><li>Use illegal drugs or consume alcohol while performing work where prohibited.</li><li>Carry weapons or dangerous items without lawful authority.</li><li>Damage Employer property.</li><li>Disclose confidential business information.</li><li>Upload malicious software or harmful code.</li><li>Attempt unauthorized access to the Platform.</li><li>Violate applicable laws.</li><li>Violation of these provisions may result in account suspension, termination, legal action, or reporting to appropriate authorities.</li></ul>
            <h3 id="sec-28">28. Workplace Conduct and Safety</h3>
            <p>Workers agree to:</p>
            <ul><li>Follow reasonable workplace safety instructions.</li><li>Use required personal protective equipment (PPE) where provided or required.</li><li>Immediately report unsafe working conditions, accidents, injuries, or emergencies to the Employer and, where appropriate, through the Platform.</li><li>Refrain from engaging in violence, harassment, intimidation, theft, or other misconduct at the workplace.</li></ul>
            <p>If a Worker believes that continuing an assignment would expose them to an immediate and serious risk to health or safety, they should notify the Employer and, where possible, inform Kaarigar through the Platform or support channels.</p>
            <h3 id="sec-29">29. Suspension or Termination of Worker Account</h3>
            <p>Kaarigar may suspend, restrict, or terminate a Worker account where it reasonably believes that the Worker has:</p>
            <ul><li>Violated these Terms.</li><li>Submitted false information.</li><li>Engaged in fraudulent or deceptive conduct.</li><li>Repeatedly cancelled accepted assignments without reasonable cause.</li><li>Failed to attend accepted assignments on multiple occasions.</li><li>Misused Platform features, including OTP verification.</li><li>Harassed or threatened other users.</li><li>Engaged in unlawful activities.</li><li>Compromised the security or integrity of the Platform.</li></ul>
            <p>Where appropriate, Kaarigar may provide the Worker with an opportunity to respond before taking permanent action, unless immediate action is necessary to protect users, comply with legal obligations, or safeguard the Platform.</p>
